# What the build context is allowed to carry.
#
# Without this file the context is the whole working tree, and two things go
# wrong. `.git` alone invalidates the build cache on every commit — the context
# hash changes whenever HEAD moves, so a docs-only commit rebuilds the wheel.
# And `scratchpad/cards/` ships sample PNGs into the build for no reason: they
# are inspection artifacts, never inputs to it.
#
# Everything here is excluded from the context, not from the image: the wheel is
# built from `src/`, `pyproject.toml` and `README.md`, and nothing below is one
# of those.

# Version control — the cache-invalidation problem above.
.git
.gitignore

# Local environments and build output. A host `.venv` holds Linux-incompatible
# or simply stale binaries and must never be confused with the image's /opt/venv.
.venv
dist/
build/
*.egg-info

# Caches: large, machine-local, and meaningless inside the image.
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Rendered cards and reports for visual inspection, plus the default --output
# directory. These are outputs of the tool, not inputs to its build.
scratchpad/
report/

# Datasets. Never committed, but they live in the tree during a real run and are
# the largest thing that could accidentally enter the context.
*.csv
_datasets/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Docker's own files: changing the Dockerfile already busts the cache without
# being part of the context it describes.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
